# Free Community Meditation — public caption rules

## Hard rule (Founder — Aug 9, 2026) — never name who leads

Public captions (Today / week_ahead / tuesday_meditation / afternoon if meditation)
must **never** name the facilitator. No Amber, Eve, Andre, etc.

Only say that there **is** meditation:

- Title: `Free Community Meditation`
- When: `Tuesday night 7:00–8:00 PM` (`session_display` in settings)
- `All are welcome`
- `No sign-up needed`
- `Doors close at 7:05pm` (`doors_close_display`)

`config/meditation_hosts.json` is **ops/internal only** — not for captions.
If TEC title/description includes a facilitator name, strip it via
`marketing.meditation.public_meditation_title` / `strip_facilitator_names`.

Paid / named workshops (massage, tarot, special events like Lions Gate) are different —
this rule is for community / Free Community Meditation.

## Doors close

**Doors close at 7:05pm** (no o'clock). Not 8:05pm.

## Single source of truth

- Config: `config/settings.json` → `tuesday_community_meditation`
  - `doors_close_display` = `"7:05pm"`
  - `session_display` = `"Tuesday night 7:00–8:00 PM"`
- Caption block built only via `marketing.meditation.meditation_event_block()`
- Used by morning tomorrow-horizon (when meditation is listed), week-ahead, and Tuesday 4pm
  `tuesday_meditation` — not Lions Gate / other free community events unless they match
  `title_match_any`

## Do not

- Hardcode `8:05` / `8:05pm` / `Doors close at …` in captions, tests, or agent instructions
- Drift between campaign paths — always go through `meditation_event_block`
- Use "o'clock" on the doors-close line
- Put `With [Name]` / facilitator names in meditation captions or tuesday openers
